1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:11,240
The human body is a physical wonder.

2
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,240
It's a machine of unfathomable complexity.

3
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,140
But it has its limits.

4
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:22,400
Superheroes play to our dreams of shedding those limits.

5
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:25,240
And we relish the fantasy.

6
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:29,980
But the fantasy is becoming reality.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,800
as today's science and technology are catching up to yesterday's science fiction.

8
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:37,900
Take super strength.

9
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,920
Now anyone can achieve it just by buckling into a super-powered exoskeleton,

10
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:49,360
built by the engineers at Raytheon Sarcos in Salt Lake City, Utah.

11
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:53,400
Their work is funded by the U.S. Army,

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,680
which envisions not only making its soldiers stronger,

13
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:59,860
but also increasing their endurance and lethality.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,840
Oh, it's way cool.

15
00:01:01,841 --> 00:01:06,000
This thing is incredibly powerful and it follows your every move,

16
00:01:06,001 --> 00:01:09,000
