132
00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:49,000
He wanted the super ability

133
00:07:49,001 --> 00:07:50,260
to control them remotely,

134
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:53,000
using the power of his mind.

135
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:56,080
So, it was back under the knife.

136
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:59,240
This was implanted in my left arm.

137
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:02,600
The implant itself consists of 100

138
00:08:02,601 --> 00:08:04,700
very, very small electrodes,

139
00:08:04,701 --> 00:08:07,840
and these were fired into my nervous system.

140
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:10,900
We can still see that the scars from the operating,

141
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:14,920
There were then wires running from there,

142
00:08:14,921 --> 00:08:18,920
all up the inside of my arm, coming out at this point here.

143
00:08:18,921 --> 00:08:24,920
And what we did was connect on this little gauntlet arrangement.

144
00:08:24,921 --> 00:08:28,920
This is actually a radio transmitter receiver unit,

145
00:08:28,921 --> 00:08:32,920
which from this terminal pad here linked to my nervous system

146
00:08:32,921 --> 00:08:37,920
and by radio, my brain signals were brought outside my body.

147
00:08:37,921 --> 00:08:39,920
So when I moved my hand, my...

148
00:08:39,921 --> 00:08:44,960
my nervous system signals were sent out to this robot hand here.

149
00:08:44,961 --> 00:08:50,680
So as I moved my hand, my brain signals were controlling this robot hand.

150
00:08:50,681 --> 00:08:57,240
But also signals from the computer could be sent down onto my nervous system for my brain to pick up.

151
00:08:57,241 --> 00:09:01,680
So I could feel how much force the robot hand was applying.

152
00:09:01,681 --> 00:09:07,920
One of Warwick's greatest challenges was to simply recognize those signals.

153
00:09:07,921 --> 00:09:11,220
But six weeks of effort got him over the hump.

154
00:09:11,221 --> 00:09:16,920
What we had done essentially was open up a new path into my brain via the implant.

155
00:09:16,921 --> 00:09:22,920
We could then put electric pulses down onto my nervous system for my brain to understand.

156
00:09:22,921 --> 00:09:28,920
What it felt like was every time a pulse came in where there was actually an electric pulse,

157
00:09:28,921 --> 00:09:31,920
it was like a charge running up my index finger.

158
00:09:31,921 --> 00:09:34,920
The more pulses, the more force.

159
00:09:34,921 --> 00:09:40,920
Warwick's implanted ship also allowed him to exercise mind control over other machines,

160
00:09:40,921 --> 00:09:42,920
like this wheelchair.

161
00:09:42,921 --> 00:09:48,920
But the path to superpowers by fusing man and machine cuts both ways.

162
00:09:48,921 --> 00:09:51,920
Instead of computerizing a human,

163
00:09:51,921 --> 00:09:54,920
you can also humanize a robot.

164
00:09:54,921 --> 00:09:59,920
This robot represents a baby step in this revolutionary concept.

165
00:09:59,921 --> 00:10:03,920
Via a Bluetooth wireless connection, it's under the control of cells extracted.

166
00:10:03,921 --> 00:10:05,920
from the brain of a rat.

167
00:10:05,921 --> 00:10:08,920
The output from the rat brain is then used

168
00:10:08,921 --> 00:10:10,920
to drive the wheels of the robot.

169
00:10:10,921 --> 00:10:14,920
The only controlling mechanism is the biological brain

170
00:10:14,921 --> 00:10:18,920
with about 100,000 brain cells.

171
00:10:18,921 --> 00:10:21,920
The extracted cells have been deposited on a petri dish,

172
00:10:21,921 --> 00:10:24,920
where they continue to send electrical impulses.

173
00:10:24,921 --> 00:10:28,920
They start to develop spontaneously connections,

174
00:10:28,921 --> 00:10:32,920
and once they connect together into a

175
00:10:32,921 --> 00:10:38,920
a network then start to communicate with each other so to speak.

176
00:10:38,921 --> 00:10:44,920
Electrodes embedded in the dish detect this communication and transfer it to the robot.

177
00:10:44,921 --> 00:10:51,920
Even though the crude neurological activity is just a faint shadow of the rat's fully functional brain,

